WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:16.420
Welcome to another Game of Thrones prequel
video in which we continue to talk about its

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:20.750
main characters, this time about Aegon ll
Targaryen.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:24.520
If you watched any of my previous videos,
you probably know when and what about this

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:28.700
Game of Thrones prequel series is going to
be about, but for those that don't,

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:32.860
let me explain it to you in short notes:
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:38.390
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president
to air in 2022. It’s based on George RR

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:42.520
Martin’s book Fire And Blood volume 1
and on Martin’s yet unfinished Fire And

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.070
Blood volume 2 book.
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:49.820
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, the creator
of the Iron Throne,

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:54.219
and goes on to recount the generations of
Targaryens who fought to hold that iconic

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:57.089
seat,
all the way up to the civil war that nearly

00:00:57.089 --> 00:01:02.079
tore their dynasty apart.”
That's Fire And Blood volume 1. The yet unreleased

00:01:02.079 --> 00:01:06.050
Fire And Blood volume 2
will continue from where part 1 ended, with

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:11.190
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, the war

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:15.780
with Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King
and Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.980
dynasty.
The key event of the prequel will be the Dance

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:24.390
of the Dragon, a Targaryen civil war.
This summer it was reported and recently confirmed

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:28.610
by Entertainment Weekly that HBO has released
a casting call for Prince who will become

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:34.730
King Aegon ll Targaryen, a key figure from
this time period of the Dance of the Dragons.

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:39.050
The casting call describes him: “Princess
Rhaenyra’s younger half-brother who challenges

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:42.340
Rhaenyra’s claim to the throne, igniting
a civil war.”

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:47.830
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve
as showrunners and executive producers.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:51.420
George R. R. Martin will also serve as executive
producer.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:55.770
The Dance of the Dragons was the most devastating
war in the history of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:02:02.120
A war of succession between Aegon II and his
half-sister Rhaenyra over their father Viserys

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:05.450
I's throne.
Both of them thought they belonged on the

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:08.310
Iron Throne.
When people started declaring for one of them

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:13.940
or the other, their fight divided the kingdoms
in two. Targaryens fought Targaryens, brothers

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:19.640
fought brothers, dragons fought dragons.
By the time it was over, thousands were dead.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:23.940
The conflict would prove to be incredibly
destructive for not only House Targaryen,

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:29.780
but large parts of Westeros as well. In addition,
it devastated Targaryen's dragon population,

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:35.130
ultimately leading to their extinction within
a few decades. They never truly recovered.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:39.900
By the end of the reign of King Viserys I
Targaryen, twenty dragons were alive.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:44.170
The majority of these died during the civil
war called the Dance of the Dragons,

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:49.210
which began in 129 AC and lasted until mid
131 AC.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:53.200
One of the main characters in this series
is going to be Prince Aegon who will become

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:58.600
King Aegon ll Targaryen. He was named by his
mother after Aegon the Conqueror.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:02.510
He's called Aegon the Usurper by supporters
of Rhaenyra Targaryen,

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:06.950
and Aegon the Elder to distinguish from Aegon
the Younger, Rhaenyra's son.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:12.110
Aegon II Targaryen was the sixth Targaryen
king to sit the Iron Throne, succeeding his

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:15.230
father,
Viserys I Targaryen, as Lord of the Seven

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:20.580
Kingdoms. His ascent was disputed by his older
half-sister, Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen,

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:26.190
who had been their father's designated heir.
Aegon and Rhaenyra fought for the throne in

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:29.520
the civil war the singers called the Dance
of the Dragons.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.210
His dragon was Sunfyre, also known as "the
Golden".

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:37.420
During the Dance, Aegon took a three-headed
golden dragon for his personal sigil

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:42.720
instead of the red three-headed Targaryen
dragon, indicating his mount.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:47.130
Aegon's supporters used his personal heraldry
as their battle-flag.

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:51.920
He wore the iron-and-ruby crown of Aegon I
Targaryen and carried Blackfyre,

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:56.790
his namesake's Valyrian steel sword.
Aegon was severely injured during the Dance

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:02.680
of the Dragons, which left him bent and twisted.
At Rook's Rest, Aegon broke his ribs, his

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:08.040
hip, and was burned on of half his body,
most severely on his left arm. His burns turned

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:11.530
to scars,
and his subsequent use of milk of the poppy

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:13.970
gave him a puffy face.

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:18.239
Later at Dragonstone, Aegon broke both his
legs and was for the remainder of his life

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:21.870
unable to walk.
Although he was not the first child of King

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:26.500
Viserys I Targaryen,
Aegon was the firstborn son of King Viserys

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:32.050
and Queen Alicent Hightower
when she gave birth to him in 106 AC. Aegon

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:37.460
II had two younger brothers, Prince Aemond
and Prince Daeron, as well as a sister, Princess

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:40.870
Helaena.
As per traditions of House Targaryen, Aegon

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:46.470
would marry his sister Helaena in 122 AC.
Together, Aegon and Helaena would have three

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:50.180
children.
The twins Prince Jaehaerys and Princess Jaehaera

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:55.910
were born in 123 AC,
and Prince Maelor was born in 127 AC. None

00:04:55.910 --> 00:05:00.860
of his children lived to adulthood,
and his line ended with Jaehaera's death in

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:04.650
133 AC.
Although he was Viserys' eldest son, Viserys

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.680
had named his eldest child and daughter his
heir,

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:13.950
Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen, Aegon's half-sister.
Rhaenyra and her children by Ser Laenor Velaryon

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:18.150
and Prince Daemon Targaryen
were to come before Aegon's own, conflicting

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:22.100
with precedents set by the Great Council of
101 AC.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:26.889
Rhaenyra had officially been appointed as
Viserys's heir in late 105 AC,

00:05:26.889 --> 00:05:30.330
with hundreds of lords and landed knights
having done obeisance to her

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:33.500
and having sworn solemn oaths to defend her
rights.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:38.450
In his life, King Viserys named Rhaenyra his
heir and his will after his death stated the

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:41.840
same,
he wanted his eldest child, Princess Rhaenyra

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.990
to succeed him.
The ensuring debate and struggle over the

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.860
succession gave birth to the Dance of the
Dragons

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:53.690
when Viserys died in 129 AC.
Ultimately, Aegon II reigned as a king, although

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:56.600
he would be succeeded by Prince Aegon the
Younger,

00:05:56.600 --> 00:06:01.340
his nephew by Rhaenyra and Daemon.
Relations at court began to escalate as lords

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:06.710
began to side with either Alicent or Rhaenyra,
with many favoring the laws established at

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:11.600
the Great Council of 101 AC,
declaring that the Iron Throne could not pass

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:14.470
to a woman.
The two parties soon became known as the "greens"

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:17.650
and the "blacks",
the former consisting of those in favor of

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:21.910
Aegon inheriting the Iron Throne,
while the latter favored Rhaenyra.

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:28.520
When King Viserys I Targaryen died in 129
AC, Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen was still

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:33.660
the heir to the Iron Throne. Since she was
pregnant at Dragonstone when her father died,

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:38.020
the greens in King's Landing hid the news
of Viserys's death, keeping the king's body

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:42.410
in his room for seven days,
until their preparations for Aegon's coronation

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:45.930
were complete.
With the exception of Lord Lyman Beesbury,

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:50.610
the small council agreed to crown Aegon.
According to Mushroom, the prince was found

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:54.990
with a young girl in Flea Bottom,
while Septon Eustace claimed Aegon was found

00:06:54.990 --> 00:07:00.460
abed with a paramour, the daughter of a trader.
According to Eustace, Aegon at first refused

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:03.580
to be a part of his mother's plans to crown
him,

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:08.300
insisting Rhaenyra was heir. However, Ser
Criston Cole, Lord Commander of the Kingsguard,

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:13.400
convinced him that should Rhaenyra take the
throne, Aegon and his brothers would be executed.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:17.650
Eustace insists that only this persuaded him
to take the crown.

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:23.150
On the tenth day of the third moon of 129
AC, the death of King Viserys I was finally

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:27.890
announced to the Seven Kingdoms and Aegon
was declared a king.

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:31.000
Preparations were made to have the coronation
at the Dragonpit.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:35.240
On the appointed day, Ser Criston the Kingmaker
placed the crown of Aegon the Conqueror upon

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:40.729
the prince's head, proclaiming him King of
the Andals, the Rhoynar, and the First Men.

00:07:40.729 --> 00:07:45.911
However, King Aegon faced the first betrayal
the same day when Ser Steffon Darklyn of the

00:07:45.911 --> 00:07:50.699
Kingsguard fled to Rhaenyra at Dragonstone
with the crown of Viserys I.

00:07:50.699 --> 00:07:55.960
Rhaenyra refused to be denied her crown, disputing
Aegon's ascension.

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:59.699
Aegon enjoyed the wealth of King's Landing,
Oldtown, and Lannisport,

00:07:59.699 --> 00:08:03.419
as well as the support of Houses Hightower,
Lannister, and Baratheon.

00:08:03.419 --> 00:08:07.610
He also maintained the appearance of legitimacy,
with the Conqueror's crown,

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:11.259
the Valyrian steel sword Blackfyre, and the
Iron Throne.

00:08:11.259 --> 00:08:17.009
Upon hearing of Rhaenyra's coronation, Aegon
demanded the heads of her and Prince Daemon,

00:08:17.009 --> 00:08:19.720
although Grand Maester Orwyle convinced Aegon
to allow him to

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:20.971
give peace terms to Rhaenyra.

00:08:20.971 --> 00:08:26.669
However, Rhaenyra refused the terms, much
to the anger of Aegon.

00:08:26.669 --> 00:08:31.150
The realm was split in two as the greens and
the blacks battled for the Iron Throne,

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:34.050
and the civil war known as the Dance of the
Dragons began.

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:39.130
Early in the war, Prince Aemond slew Prince
Lucerys Velaryon over Storm's End,

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:44.800
while Lucerys was attempting to win Borros
Baratheon, Lord of Storm's End, over to his

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:50.290
mother's side. Upon Aemond's return, having
ensured Storm's End's support, Aegon welcomed

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:55.240
his brother with a great feast, although Queen
Alicent and her father, Ser Otto Hightower,

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:59.120
the Hand of the King,
were concerned about the extent of Aemond's

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:02.120
actions.
Seeking revenge against Aegon, Prince Daemon

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:07.700
took action. Aegon's heir, Prince Jaehaerys,
was killed in the Red Keep by Blood and Cheese,

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:13.440
agents of Mysaria, Daemon's spymaster.
While Blood was captured and tortured to death,

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:18.120
Cheese who was a ratcatcher was not found.
In his fury, Aegon ordered every ratcatcher

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:21.890
in the city to be hanged.
While the greens suffered a series of defeats

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:27.060
in the riverlands, Ser Otto attempted to win
allies with letters and buying sellswords.

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:31.210
Aegon mistook his efforts for inaction, and
his caution for cowardice.

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:36.760
With House Velaryon, House Stark, House Arryn,
and many of the riverlords firmly behind his

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:40.170
sister, Aegon drowned his growing fears in
strongwine.

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:45.680
With Corlys Velaryon, Lord of the Tides, blockading
King's Landing, Otto reached out to the Triarchy

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:51.110
and Dalton Greyjoy, Lord of the Iron Islands,
for aid. Because of his grandfather's delays

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:54.830
in waging war,
Aegon stripped Otto of the Handship and awarded

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:59.220
it to Criston Cole.
Ser Criston soon took to the offensive.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:03.880
Aegon himself took the field in a trap set
by the Kingmaker at Rook's Rest,

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:09.510
where he and Aemond fought and killed Princess
Rhaenys Targaryen, the Queen Who Never Was,

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:14.480
and her dragon, Meleys.
However, Sunfyre were badly maimed by Rhaenys

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:17.570
and Meleys,
and Aegon suffered from burns that covered

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:21.520
half his body, a broken hip, and numerous
broken ribs.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:26.640
His armor had melted into his left arm, and
it would take him a year to recover.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:32.130
Aemond took over the rule in his stead as
Prince Regent and Protector of the Realm.

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:36.820
Aegon remained bent and twisted for the rest
of his life, half his body covered in burn

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:39.441
scars.
Rhaenyra took King's Landing and the Iron

00:10:39.441 --> 00:10:43.940
Throne in 130 AC,
Aemond and Daemon slew each other in the Battle

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:48.130
Above the Gods Eye,
and Criston perished in the Butcher's Ball.

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:52.430
Before they could be captured by Rhaenyra,
however, Larys Strong, Lord of Harrenhal,

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:55.310
secretly smuggled Aegon and his children out
of the city.

00:10:55.310 --> 00:11:01.420
While his children were spirited away to safety,
Aegon disguised himself as one of the smallfolk

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:06.300
and escaped on a fishing boat, later arriving
on Dragonstone where he convinced several

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:11.700
blacks to defect and help him take the island.
During the fall of Dragonstone, he fought

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:16.660
Daemon's daughter, Princess Baela Targaryen,
both of them mounted on dragons.

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:20.750
When Sunfyre and Moondancer fell to the earth
during the fight,

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:24.279
Aegon tried to jump off his dragon's back,
shattering his legs.

00:11:24.279 --> 00:11:28.650
Meanwhile, Aegon's wife Helaena had ended
her grief by jumping out of her room in the

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:31.370
capital,
and his son, Prince Maelor, was killed by

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:35.420
a mob in Bitterbridge.
Following the Storming of the Dragonpit, Rhaenyra

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:41.050
fled to Dragonstone in 130 AC.
Unaware of Aegon's coup, she was captured

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:45.520
on arrival, judged a traitor, and fed by Aegon
to Sunfyre,

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:49.209
as Rhaenyra's surviving son, Prince Aegon
the Younger, watched.

00:11:49.209 --> 00:11:54.649
Ser Alfred Broome argued for killing Prince
Aegon as well, although the king forbade it.

00:11:54.649 --> 00:12:00.490
However the war continued as Rhaenyra's supporters
continued her cause supporting Aegon the Younger,

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:05.870
despite the boy being Aegon the Elder's prisoner.
Although Rhaenyra was dead, the Dance of the

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:09.220
Dragons was not yet over
as those loyal to her continued the fight

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:13.930
in the name of her son Aegon the Younger.
The river-lords marched towards King's Landing,

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:18.580
while a large host from the Vale of Arryn
was hiring ships to bring them down on the

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:22.589
capital.
Aegon made efforts to hatch dragon eggs from

00:12:22.589 --> 00:12:27.740
Dragonstone, but to no success.
Although Aegon II desired for his sister's

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:30.959
line to end;
Aegon decreed that the prince would either

00:12:30.959 --> 00:12:36.470
join the Night's Watch or serve him as a eunuch.
With armies closing in on the capital and

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:40.510
his lords plotting and arguing, Aegon II remained
oblivious.

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:45.480
However, Kermit Tully, Lord of Riverrun, and
his army had defeated Lord Borros Baratheon

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:49.890
in the Battle of the Kingsroad.
With no green armies remaining, the Lads marching

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:52.890
on the capital,
and with the additional approach of the Valemen

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:58.110
and the northern army of Cregan Stark,
Lord of Winterfell, Lord Corlys Velaryon knew

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:03.650
defeat was imminent in 131 AC.
He counseled King Aegon to abdicate and join

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:08.459
the Night's Watch, but the king refused.
He instead gave orders to have the ear of

00:13:08.459 --> 00:13:13.330
his nephew, Prince Aegon the Younger,
cut off and sent to Lord Tully as a warning.

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:17.930
After his meeting with the small council,
the fatigued Aegon climbed into his litter

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:23.030
and asked to be carried to the royal sept.
The king had his customary flagon of sweet

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:27.881
Arbor red along the way to ease his pain.
When his escort arrived and a Knight of the

00:13:27.881 --> 00:13:32.880
Kingsguard lifted the litter's curtains,
Aegon II was found dead with blood on his

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:37.440
lips.
With Aegon II dead, Lord Corlys and an unharmed

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:41.010
Aegon the Younger
rode out to meet the vanguard of Kermit Tully's

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:45.960
host, proclaiming the king was dead.
The late king had no male heirs left, which

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:50.990
led to his nephew Aegon the Younger,
Rhaenyra's son, ascending to the Iron Throne.

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:55.399
Who exactly poisoned the king remains unknown,
although those judged responsible

00:13:55.399 --> 00:13:58.389
were arrested for the crime during the Hour
of the Wolf

00:13:58.389 --> 00:14:04.139
when Lord Cregan Stark took over the capital.
Even though Lord Stark was on Rhaenyra's side,

00:14:04.139 --> 00:14:08.060
he still wanted those who broke their loyalty
towards Aegon ll punished

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:12.250
because they could do the same in the future
to Rhaenyra's son Aegon lll.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:17.410
The main susects in Aegon II's death were
Lord Velaryon, Lord Larys Strong,

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:21.600
and Ser Perkin the Flea, who feared that Aegon
II remaining on the Iron Throne

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:27.760
would lead to continued war. Lord Stark had
26 traitors arrested, judged and punished

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:31.040
or spared.
It's often agreed by many that no one really

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:35.029
won the Dance of the Dragons,
but it's a fact that Rhaenyra's loyalists

00:14:35.029 --> 00:14:38.670
won the war and Rhaenyra's children got the
throne.

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:43.200
Despite being considered as part of the Targaryen
dynasty, history would not be kind to Aegon

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:46.710
II,
even though it's equally unkind to his half-sister,

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:49.220
Rhaenyra.
Thank you so much for watching!

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:56.709
If you enjoyed this video please give it a
big thumbs up and I hope to see you in the

00:14:56.709 --> 00:14:58.759
next one!
Peace!

